WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.930
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.850
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.400
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.790
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:18.780
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.960
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.470
dokoka tooku de mimi wo sumashiteru hito ga iru
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:40.390
Yakitate!! Japan

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:40.400
arayuru basho de sora wo miageteru hito ga iru
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:47.030
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.
arayuru basho de sora wo miageteru hito ga iru

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:54.910
yozora no shita de kuchibue fuiteru bokutachi wa
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:02.620
kotoba mo nai mama yubi de tada seiza wo nazotteru
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:10.090
samugariya no yume tsumetai kimi no te
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:19.470
atatameru mahou wa hitotsu no michi wo shinjiru koto
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:28.230
houkigumo no mukou ni mitsuketa hitotsubu no hoshi wa
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.490
kagayaku hoshi demo kasukana hoshi demo
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.450
kimi dake no hikari
is the light of only you.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.230
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:44.040
is a sign post that remains unseen.
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:51.760
saa kono te wo hiraite ima nani wo shinjimasuka?
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.960
A young boy who has awakened to
bread-making, Azuma Kazuma,

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.840
has those extraordinarily warm hands which
are ideal for making dough ferment,

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.720
otherwise known as Solar Hands.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.350
Now in pursuit of Japan’s original bread, <i>Japan</i>,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.440
he has decided to take the challenge of the
new employee examination at Pantasia,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.480
Tokyo’s highest-ranking bakery.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.310
Azuma Kazuma, eh?

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.440
You’re five minutes late.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.070
Five point deduction!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:16.980
What the...?

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.740
This marked the beginning of his career.
What the...?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.070
This marked the beginning of his career.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.490
There will be only one person
chosen out of the 35 here.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.700
One?

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.580
Whoa, this is really serious.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.540
But that’s okay, I’ll just do my best until the end.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.790
Yeah!

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.250
Maharajah!!

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.050
The Day Mount Fuji Fell!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.090
I won’t lose!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.800
I’ll fight with <i>Japan</i>!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.800
Which part of the country are you from?

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.260
You’re quite carefree, aren’t you?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.220
Do you understand how difficult it is,

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.510
to be recruited by Pantasia?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.810
Mr. “Minus Five Points.”

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:50.940
Huh?

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:51.900
Listen up.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.150
Pantasia is the charisma
of the bakery world.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.280
Merely being able to work here...

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.700
It’s recognized by everyone to
be something prestigious.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.240
What’s more, you may even be placed
in charge of your own store!

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.290
It’s the same as being
a winner in this world!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.250
What’s with that indifferent reaction?!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.840
Well, it can’t be helped, I have
no interest in such things.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.050
Wha...?

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.380
The reason I came to Japan’s number one bread shop...

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.050
is because I thought I could find a hint.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.560
It’s because I thought I might find an opportunity.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.890
An opportunity to know the true
form of the new <i>Japan</i>...

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.100
That’s all!

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.020
Hey!

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.280
Don’t make idle talk!

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.520
I’m really sorry!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.820
I’m just so happy we were able to reunite
under such nostalgic circumstances.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.780
I don’t know you!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.540
What’re you saying?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.290
It’s me, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.920
What’re you doing?!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.600
You have something good, don’t you?

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.060
You. You. You.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.610
10 point deduction.
You can go home now.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.610
W-What’s this?

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.900
I don’t understand the reason.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.110
It’s simple.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.360
Nose hair!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.740
The stench of sweat!

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.610
Railroad haircut!

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:29.580
No way, no way!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.780
In short, you’re all lacking in cleanliness.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.620
We have no use for people like you.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.990
N-No way!

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.380
Don’t be ridiculous!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.590
He’s a person who says cruel things easily, isn’t he?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.880
Number 35.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:44.840
That’s me.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.340
Two point deduction.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.600
Why?!

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.630
Your hair is messy.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:51.760
It looks unclean.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.600
I-I’m unclean?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.600
Why don’t you stop doing that?

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.400
For instance...

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.570
If there’s someone with messy hair...

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.580
See?

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.530
Now it’s okay.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.410
It’s easily fixed.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.080
Isn’t it?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.410
It’s troublesome for you
to do as you please.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.590
It should be fine.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.090
Or will you fail me with a 10 point deduction?

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.840
Failing is not the issue here... little girl.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.470
What exactly are you planning?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.350
No matter what happens, I’ll enforce the rules.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.810
Point deduction remains.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:38.730
Stingy.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.940
For the first part of the new employee
examination, naturally,

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.400
I will have you make bread.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.700
You are free to make whatever you want.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:53.450
However, household breads such as savory
bread and sweetened buns are not allowed.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.240
Use of mixers is also prohibited.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.620
You must all knead the dough with your own hands.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.620
I’m sure you already know,

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.410
but this examination is to test the foundation
of your bread-making skills.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.420
If you need any other special ingredients, ask now.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.130
Yes.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.390
In that case... I’d like some ascorbic
acid, and some malt.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.970
That cutie intends to make French bread.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.890
Rye wheat.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.890
For that guy, it’s probably German bread.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.640
Wow, you sure know a lot.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.020
It’s more like you don’t know anything.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.770
Are you really interested in becoming a baker?

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.770
But you see, I’ve only ever made <i>Japan</i>.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.320
So, like, what’s that <i>Japan</i> thing?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.000
I’ve never seen nor heard of it.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.410
I’ll show you after this.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.000
<i>Japan</i> #56.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.790
Time limit is three hours.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.000
Part one of the new employee examination begins now!

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.480
1 hour’s progress
First fermentation

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.310
Seems like it’s expanding well.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.780
I’ll let out the gas in 3 minutes and 30 seconds.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.400
What’s with that dough?

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.120
That speed of fermentation isn’t normal.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.530
Those extraordinarily warm hands that
maintain the ideal dough temperature

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.120
for yeast germ fermentation...

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.460
There’s no mistake about this guy...

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.460
He possesses Solar Hands.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.340
What’s wrong?

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:33.050
Well, boy... You mentioned some
Japan number thing before?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.380
<i>Japan</i> #56.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:38.470
In that case, you have others, right?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.180
I do. For example...

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:43.190
this is <i>Japan</i> #55.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.730
T-This...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.690
was made by Solar Hands...

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.790
T-This is...?

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:01.780
What deliciousness!

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.790
This sweetness isn’t from the bean jam...

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.290
The anko itself is retaining its own sweetness.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.960
The dough... The bread dough is drawing
out the natural sweetness of wheat!

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:13.170
Soft, yet firm to the touch...

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.970
The construction of this dough...

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.430
You made this by yugone seihou,
didn’t you?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.220
“Yogore”...? I haven’t done anything like that.
Note: Kazuma misheard the word as “yogore,” which means dirt.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:24.060
I just kneaded the dough
with hot water,

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.690
let it sit for a whole day,
then fermented it.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.350
If you do that,

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:31.780
the dough matures, and the natural
sweetness of wheat is drawn out.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.160
Like I said, that’s what you call “yugone seihou.”

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:40.070
But with this dough, whether the filling
is bean jam, cream or chocolate,

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.280
it becomes a perfectly matched <i>Japan</i>.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.700
In that case, why not just call it
a sweetened bun, like normal?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.790
<i>Japan</i> is <i>Japan</i>!

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.750
Oh crap, this isn’t the time for me to be doing this!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.420
It’s time to let out the gas!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.680
Dough shaping
2 hours’ progress

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:03.350
This guy’s a moron, but his hands are the real thing.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.470
<i>Japan</i> #56...

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.060
I don’t know what might happen.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.560
“Hammer in what sticks out.”

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.070
“If you have a problem,
spread it around.”

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:13.700
Hey.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:16.030
Hey.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.450
What is it?

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.370
Success! Rolling-pin-slip plan, bingo!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.460
Are you all right, boy?

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.590
I stepped on something and fell.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.130
No, my dough!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.680
Oops.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.980
Sorry. There were absolutely no ill intentions.

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.560
I just thought I’d pick your rolling pin up for you...

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.480
I know, don’t worry about it.
I’ll remake it.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:53.310
I-In that case... it’s all good.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.230
Though I said that...

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.320
I only have one hour left.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:00.740
If I were to start over again now,

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.160
adding more yeast germ to speed up the
fermentation would be all that I can do.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.660
But in that case...

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.790
it’ll be a dried out, tasteless bread.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.620
Point deduction is certain.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.670
This time I decidedly...

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.680
give up on #56.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.630
Excuse me! Do you have any yogurt?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.550
What?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.010
Yogurt, he says?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.270
N-No way... surely he’s not considering using
bifidus bacteria instead of yeast germ?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:26.810
Okay.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.110
Bread made with yogurt...

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.310
I’ve heard of if, but...

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.320
Oh well... he won’t be able to make
a decent bread, anyway.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.700
Most people have reached the final shaping stage.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:45.070
That’s French bread, but it’s of a medium size...

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.370
A batard.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.040
The crispness of the crust is the lifeblood
of proper French bread...

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.340
However...

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.660
Azusagawa Tsukino,

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.340
a batard should be a cinch for you.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.470
Looks good, doesn’t it?

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.890
Hey, stand back a bit.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.510
Why?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.770
If you don’t want to get injured, stay back.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.350
S-Sword rolling pin?!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.940
Who on earth is this guy?

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.440
So he’s making roggenbrot?

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:18.520
Roggen.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.450
In other words, German bread made with rye wheat.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.700
It’s a difficult bread, but I can tell without
seeing the end result that he’s done a good job.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:27.110
Suwabara Kai...

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:31.210
Will someone capable of surpassing
him really appear in this exam?

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.200
Looking around...

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:37.210
I see just two people approaching this
with a different sense of purpose.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Number 34, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.510
Number 35, Azuma Kazuma.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.180
What in the world are they making?

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.560
Hmm? What is that dumpling?

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.850
Right! Now I just have to bake it!
Right! Now I just have to bake it!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:52.780
What?! No way!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.890
T-This is <i>Japan</i>?

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:56.780
Is that the national flag?

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.480
It definitely looks like the rising-sun flag, but...

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.030
Is this why he calls it <i>Japan</i>?

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.280
What’s this guy thinking?!

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.490
Temperature will be 250°C.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.500
30 minutes.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:12.000
30 minutes until <i>Japan</i> completion!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.840
It seems like everyone’s finished with their baking.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.560
So... what’s going on with his bread?

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.820
It’s bothering me.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.520
It’s been 30 minutes already.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:44.320
Hey! Don’t just open it yourself!

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.030
Empty!

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.780
You’re messing with me,
aren’t you? Moron!

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:53.370
Like I said, it was
a bit too early to open it.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.040
That’s got nothing to do with it.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.750
Just now, a sound...

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.300
F-Fuu...

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.800
Mount Fuji... Mount Fuji fell down.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.670
Moreover, what a splendid Mount Fuji.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.010
The white on top looks like snow,

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.270
and the browned areas look like the mountain surface.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.770
B-But, when I saw it before...

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.390
it was shaped like a flag.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:19.780
How on earth did it...?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.030
It can’t be, where is that dumpling?

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:25.780
I can’t see it.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.030
There it is! It’s stuck up there.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.280
What’s going on?

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.290
After I ruined his dough, he started
baking within 20 minutes.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.500
He didn’t let it ferment?

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.550
That’s a non-rising bread, <i>Japan</i> #16.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.710
<i>Japan</i> #16?

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.380
That aside, is your bread okay?

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.510
Crap!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.220
That’s all!

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.400
I will now begin the scoring.

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:12.660
Number 1,

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.070
minus 10.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.160
Number 2, minus 10 as well.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.410
Number 3, minus 6.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.370
Oh, no.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.200
Number 4, minus 8.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.630
Number 5, minus 8.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.760
P-Please wait.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.010
What is it?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:28.010
How can you decide the points
without even tasting them?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.220
Because that’s me!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.470
I don’t have to taste them to know!

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.310
That is all!

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.360
E-Even so, I can’t accept that.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.610
The number 1 guy and I, number 2,
both made the same butter rolls.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.450
Even by looking, the difference in quality is obvious.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.610
I cannot approve of receiving the same minus 10.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.120
Well-made bread has elasticity.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.750
If you push it with your finger,
it quickly restores its shape.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.430
But your bread...

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:04.960
doesn’t restore itself!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.060
On top of that,
its scent of yeast is weak!

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.930
That is proof that it hasn’t fermented enough.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:19.650
Your bread isn’t even worth minus
10, it deserves minus 20!

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.730
Go home, scum!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.950
That examiner occhan’s power of insight is amazing.
Note: “Occhan” is a term used in reference to older men.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.490
You, number 35! Minus two!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:32.990
Why?!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.370
I’m still 22. I’m not an occhan!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.700
Incidentally, you only have
one point left.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:40.750
No way...

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.840
You lose too many points in areas which
have nothing to do with your skill.
No way...

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.960
You lose too many points in areas which
have nothing to do with your skill.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.420
Oh dear.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.340
Pay attention, everybody!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.540
A very well-made bread...

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.180
Number 6, Suwabara, may I?

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.800
Yeah, I don’t even mind a fist.

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:56.430
Then... fist!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.570
This is the proof of real bread.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.710
Number 6, Suwabara,
zero point deduction.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.290
Number 12, minus 7.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.660
Number 13, minus 10.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.250
Number 14, minus 8.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:20.580
No!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.000
Number 34,

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.600
is this Chinese steamed bread, hua chuan?
Note: “Hua chuan” / “hua juan,” also known in English as “flower scallion rolls.”

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.510
But you have baked it.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:29.300
That’s correct.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:33.260
By baking it, the steam is sealed inside,
which results in a crisp outside

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:36.850
but fluffy inside, creating a whole new sensation.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.060
I see.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.100
But it’s a pity... Minus 2.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.860
What? D-Deduction?!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:45.400
Please try some.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.600
If it were me...

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.090
I would have baked it for 30 seconds less.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:53.530
T-That’s exactly right.

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:54.750
He saw through me.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.000
Undoubtedly, I missed the baking time.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.040
T-That’s...

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.880
Hey, that looks quite tasty.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:03.790
because I got distracted by his bread!
Hey, that looks quite tasty.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.550
because I got distracted by his bread!

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.000
Even for someone like me... To think...

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:16.010
Without tasting it
I can’t make a decision.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.180
Number 35, what exactly...

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:19.980
is this?

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.510
It’s <i>Japan</i> #16.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.350
Have some, it’s good!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.020
I don’t know how to eat this.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.400
Where do I start?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.400
You can eat it however you like.

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:31.900
As I thought, only that one...

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.400
He’s going to eat it?

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.110
W-What... is this feeling?

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.550
What is this impulse that’s welling up inside me?

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.510
It’s no use... I can’t hold it in.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.600
This is not Mount Fuji.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.340
It’s the world’s highest... Everest...

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.140
Otherwise known as Chomolungma!

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.110
And now, I’m trembling with excitement.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.820
I want to eat curry!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.280
I’ve got it!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.030
The shape is different, but this is Indian bread. It’s naan!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.490
Note: Kazuma heard it as “Nanda,” which translates to
“What’s that?” Quite a humorous mistake, which continues.
What, you say?

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.490
I’ve just been telling you, it’s <i>Japan</i> #16.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.550
No no, this is naan.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.500
I’m telling you, it’s <i>Japan</i>!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:28.750
I don’t care what it is,
but in any case, it’s naan!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.920
It’s what?! You’re talking about that?

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.510
It’s <i>Japan</i>!

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:35.840
Moron. If he says “naan,” he’s talking
about the Indian bread.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.010
That’s wrong!

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.100
While pursuing an original Japanese bread, I made this...

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.260
my 16th creation.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.430
I wanted a bread that would go well

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:48.270
with the Japanese curry that I loved
since I was a kid, so I made it.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.570
Curry is Japanese food?

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:52.780
What’s he saying?!

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.900
You really are a moron.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.820
Curry is Indian food.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.400
You’re the moron.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.780
Curry is spicy, which is why it’s called curry.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.700
“Karai” is a Japanese word, right?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.580
But, it’s not Japanese food...

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.300
What kind of basis is that?!

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:10.790
And so I made if to look like the
symbol of Japan, Mount Fuji.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.210
Good idea, isn’t it?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.340
But there’s a real reason
behind this shape...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.090
The real way to eat it...

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.970
is to turn it upside-down, like this...

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.640
and pour loads of curry into it.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.400
To guzzle if like this, it’s really quite delicious.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.650
I don’t care about how it’s eaten.
There’s something else I want to ask.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.490
That circular dumpling,

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.410
why was it stuck to the top of the oven?

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.540
You don’t eat that?

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.410
That’s a clump of flour.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.040
It’s kind of like a glue that’s used to hold
the dough to the top of the oven.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.540
As the bond gradually loosens,

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:55.840
the dough browns, and the part that’s
stuck to the flour becomes the snow.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.260
And finally, it loses to the weight of the dough and falls.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:03.300
This is something I thought of when I was 10,
while looking at a teru-teru-bouzu.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.770
In the beginning I used yeast germ,

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:10.020
but the dough would expand while baking,

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.270
so I tried making it without fermenting.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.270
When I also added yogurt,

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:17.570
its slight acidity went really
well with curry.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.080
It really was quite good when I tried it.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:22.620
Well,

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:27.620
that’s basically why I decided to try this one,
and save time with a non-rising bread.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.160
So, what about my score?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:32.930
The score...

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.380
Plus two!

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.430
Someone finally got a positive score!

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.180
He’s saying that it’s better than my roggenbrot?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.630
Something like that...

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.020
<i>Japan</i> #16, huh?

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:47.760
It’s kind of exciting, isn’t it?

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.970
I don’t have any comments regarding the shape...

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.310
but the taste was the real thing.

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.740
I honestly thought it tasted good.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:58.380
Number 35, Azuma Kazuma...

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:01.320
This guy may have extensive skills.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.840
Number 6, Suwabara Kai.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.050
Number 11, Azusagawa Tsukino.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.550
Number 34, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.260
Number 35, Azuma Kazuma.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.800
The rest may leave.

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:15.340
No, just leave!
There will be no discussion!

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:17.050
I still have points left!

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:17.970
Me too!

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:18.750
And me!

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.800
In that case, all of you get minus 10!

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:24.240
He’s a demon!

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:29.050
For the remaining four, as a final examination, I’ll assign you a common task.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.520
You’ll spend the night in this store,
and by noon tomorrow...

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:34.290
make a croissant.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.520
The new employee will be
decided by this test.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:42.500
You will choose who to employ?

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:45.800
Who will remain, other than me,
once this test is over?

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:48.780
What’s so funny, Mr. Bandana?

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:53.290
I look forward to seeing what kinds
of croissants you all make.

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:57.140
You seem awfully calm, little lady.

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:58.790
That’s not true.

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:02.680
She’s so easygoing, I can’t tell
what she may be thinking.

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:04.100
Hey, hey...

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:04.980
Hey!

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:06.190
What, already?!

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:09.200
For the next trial...
Who is this Kurowa-san?
Note: “Kurowassan” means “croissant,” but Kazuma misheard it as a person’s name.

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.060
Kurowa-san? What are you talking about?

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:13.770
Kurowa-san.

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:16.610
It’s not Kurowa-san! It’s croissant!

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.070
Everyone knows what that is, dumbass!

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:19.210
I don’t.

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:21.740
N-No way...

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:25.120
Have you really only made <i>Japan</i>?

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:25.960
Right!

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:34.180
Who in the world is Kurowa-san?

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:47.680
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:48.250 --> 00:22:56.690
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:07.700
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:12.910
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:19.010
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:21.580
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:25.720
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:30.490
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:34.330
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:39.030
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:44.200
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:53.010
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:24:02.370
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:09.330
The task for the final exam... is a croissant!

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:10.910
Who is Kurowa-san?

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:11.910
Are you a moron?

00:24:11.910 --> 00:24:14.580
It’s not Kurowa-san! It’s croissant!

00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:16.540
Next episode, Yakitate!! Japan.

00:24:16.540 --> 00:24:19.540
Burnt black!! Is this the final Kurowa-san!?

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:21.010
Be sure to see it!

00:24:21.010 --> 00:24:23.760
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:25.260
Azuma,

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:29.010
you know that an-pan was made by the Japanese at the start of the Meiji era, right?

00:24:29.010 --> 00:24:32.740
Incidentally, jam bread and cream bread are
also sweetened buns made by the Japanese.

00:24:33.450 --> 00:24:34.700
Wow.
